Z||000000||Haze_Performance||09-25-2001||01:29 AM||||I bought a Fiero part off eBay. The guy lives in Canada. I sent him a money order (from a Currency Exchange) in the correct amount, but he now says "<I>You didn't send a US POSTAL money order! What's the deal??????</I>"  Correct me if I'm worng but its the same thing. You shouldnt have any trouble cashing it. Ive bought many things from Canada using the same type payment... <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallindysig_copy.jpg">     .     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallredsig.jpg">     .     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fullstaff_1.gif"> <BR><I><B><FONT COLOR="red">Classic Fiero Owners</B></I></FONT> - <FONT COLOR="red"><A HREF="http://www.WS6Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A></FONT>||||reg||10
Z||000001||Mach10||09-25-2001||02:40 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> That doesn't matter in the slightest. It's possible, though, that his bank might be raping him for a $3.00CDN handling fee. <P>What a goat-roper  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"><P>Gimme his address. I'll send my cousin Guiedo to explain things  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_drunk.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000002||Haze_Performance||09-25-2001||03:09 AM||||He just emailed me & said "<I> I cash my money orders at the post office in Washington State! Do<BR>you think they will cash it there?????  I don't have a US bank account!  </I>"<P>As long as its in his name & he has an ID right?<P>Thanks Mach10<P><BR>-Haze   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallindysig_copy.jpg">      .      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallredsig.jpg">      .      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fullstaff_1.gif">  <BR><I><B><FONT COLOR="red">Classic Fiero Owners</B></I></FONT> - <FONT COLOR="red"><A HREF="http://www.WS6Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 09-25-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000003||maryjane||09-25-2001||03:12 AM||||I ran across a similar, but opposite occurance last week. A friend of mine buys/sells collectable fishing stuff on ebay. He sold an item to a buyer in Canada-the money order came in-the item was shipped out. My friend then found that his bank wouldn't touch the 'foriegn' money order. He contacted the buyer, requested a new and different form of payment. Was more or less told to screw off, it was a good m.o. My friend ended up sending it to a friend in Canada and got it cashed up there, mailed the<BR>cash back here. Can't blame either party for their views, i guess.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Haze_Performance||09-25-2001||04:39 AM||||BUMP  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroBUZZ||09-25-2001||09:43 AM||||Haze:  <BR>I would wonder why this guy crosses the border to cash his cheques. Trying not to leave a paper trail?<P>I guess you could refuse to accept certain payments, but a MO should be regarded as cash or a certified cheque.  It is backed by the firm issuing so unless it's Bob's Quickie Store they should be good.<P>I'm an ex Credit Union manager and have never had a problem with any US/Canada instruments (barring fraud).  I'd put it down to dealing with a weirdo!!<BR>Gary<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Wannabe||09-25-2001||09:54 AM||||A money order from a bank or other financial institution is no problem to cash in Canada. Postal money orders are another story, and are clearly marked "Negotiable only in US and Possessions" unless it is an "International" postal money order. Money Mart and some places will still cash these, but it ends up costing about $5. The currency is no problem as you do not need to have a $US account to cash a $US check or money order.||||reg||1
